#
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES
#   `.softhouse/bin/fire-program.sh` reads it as its FIRST action, before preflight and
#   before the lock, and exits non-zero without doing anything. Any fire — local launchd
#   or cloud routine — that starts from a checkout of this repository stops here.
#
# WHY IT LIVES IN THE REPO RATHER THAN ON A HOST
#   The local launchd job was unloaded on 2026-09-06 and its plist renamed. That was not
#   enough: the machine was powered off accidentally, login RELOADED the plist, a fire ran
#   as 20260906-200001, and it committed to main. A host-local stop does not survive a
#   reboot and does not reach a fire running somewhere else. This file travels with the
#   repository, so it reaches every producer that clones or pulls it.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT DO
#   It does not cancel a SCHEDULE. A cloud routine will still wake, pull, read this, and
#   refuse — burning its own time each tick. Removing the schedule is a separate action
#   that only the account owner can take.
#
# HOW TO RESTART THE PROGRAM
#   Delete this file in a commit that says why. Nothing else is disabled: no guard, no
#   instrument, no history has been removed, and `guard_program_stopped` (which refuses
#   the bar when this file coexists with a held LOCK) stops applying the moment it is gone.
